1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
In this video, I will introduce the actual hair growth function.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
In the previous version, users can only check the hair growth effect through Vray rendering.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Since the 2025.0 version, the material type in the shell has increased to a new material hair growth rate.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Users can directly create and check the hair growth effect in the 3D window without rendering,

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
thereby greatly simplifying the workflow.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
In addition, the hair that is based on Vray rendering can only be checked in the rendering window,

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
limiting its use in the external application program.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
In comparison, the hair growth rate material can lead to USD format,

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
greatly increasing the compatibility with external tools.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Currently, this function can only be used in Windows systems, and will also support Mac systems in the future.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Let's take a look at how to set the hair growth rate.

12
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
If you want to display or hide hair growth rate material in the 3D window,

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
you can put the mouse on the clothing rendering option in the switch menu,

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,000
click the icon to display the hair growth rate,

15
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
and then use the function.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
At this time, the hair growth rate material will be displayed on the fabric of the hair growth rate.

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
You can check it in the 3D window in time.

18
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,000
You can also click on the color of the hair growth rate randomly,

19
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
and assign random colors to each hair growth rate,

20
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
so that it is easier to check the various shapes of hair growth rates.

21
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,000
When you use a fabric with hair growth rate material,

22
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,000
these options will be banned and cannot be selected.

23
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
You can control the hair growth rate in the 3D window by choosing three different options.

24
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Let's go to the main menu, open the settings,

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
then open the user's definition, and click the 3D option.

26
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
In the hair growth rate form, you can see three options,

27
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
the original hair, the plane, and the limit.

28
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Click each option to display the difference in the 3D window.

29
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Selecting the original hair will display the original hair with thickness and width,

30
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
which helps to check the overall structure of the hair.

31
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Selecting the plane will display the hair with thickness but no thickness,

32
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
and the hair with thickness and width will display the hair with width but no thickness.

33
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The selected option is default.

34
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The limit shows that the hair is a simple curve,

35
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
without thickness or width.

36
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
We can select the original,

37
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
and get a more realistic appearance of the hair.

38
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Now let's see how to directly apply the hair growth rate material to the costume.

39
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Click the Fabric 1 in the object window.

40
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
In the attribute editor,

41
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
change the type of material to hair growth rate.

42
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Use the Fabric 1 fabric for the costume.

43
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
It will immediately display the hair in the 3D window.

44
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:33,000
You can also select various hair types from the following hair types.

45
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
At the bottom of the attribute editor,

46
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
just like the previous hair dye type,

47
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
you can adjust the details of the attribute,

48
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
such as parameters,

49
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
shape settings,

50
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
and default application to set the hair style.

51
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Here we will quickly adjust some of the parameter values,

52
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
to show the work principle of hair setting.

53
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Although the hair rate and hair are only dyed,

54
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,000
use the same parameters,

55
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
and set the attribute.

56
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
But in the hair dye window,

57
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
the distribution of these two hair types is different.

58
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
In the hair dye list,

59
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
a new random option has been added.

60
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
By adjusting the seed distribution value,

61
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
even if you use the same parameters,

62
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
you can also create a slightly different hair arrangement.

63
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
After setting the parameters of the hair,

64
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
now let's open the synchronized dyeing in the hair dye window,

65
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:21,000
to see the final dyeing effect of the hair.

66
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
You can also export the hair dye data created in the hole

67
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:28,000
as a usd file and use it in other software.

68
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Come to the main menu,

69
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,000
click on the file export,

70
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
select the usd format,

71
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
confirm the storage path,

72
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
enter the file name,

73
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
click on the save,

74
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
and then click on the export usd window.

75
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Ensure that the selection contains the hair dye data option,

76
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,000
so that the hair dye data is exported to the usd file.

77
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Here we show a section of the hair dye,

78
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
in the virtual engine,

79
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
used to simulate a short video.

80
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
In the 2025 version,

81
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,000
the new hair dyeing material can be used to create the same hair dye

82
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
as the 3D window and the dyeing window.

83
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
In addition,

84
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
by exporting the hair dye data,

85
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
you can also import it into other tools,

86
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
and use it in various creative projects.

